    turns [38;5;153m{page:-1}[39m from a harmless empty result into [38;5;153mslice(-20,-10)[39m, which returns items 5-14 from the [3mend[0m of the
    array. [1mThese two must be fixed together.[0m Also, [38;5;153msize[39m is unbounded.
  - [1mTest asserts length, not content ([38;5;153mtest/handlers.test.js:26[39m)[0m: [38;5;153massert.strictEqual(res.orders.length, 10)[39m passes under
    both the correct and the broken offset. I ran the suite: 2/2 pass with both criticals live. There's also no
    happy-path [38;5;153mcreateOrderHandler[39m test asserting the order actually lands in the store — that would have caught C2.
  - [1mConfig has no key validation ([38;5;153msrc/config.js:7[39m)[0m: moving from a literal to [38;5;153mconfig.json[39m is new surface. A
    present-but-incomplete file (missing [38;5;153mpageSize[39m) makes every listing return [38;5;153m{status:200, orders:[]}[39m with nothing
    logged.

  [1mWhere I'd downgrade the reviewer[0m

  [1m[38;5;153mwithRetry[39m with [38;5;153mattempts: 0[39m throws [38;5;153mundefined[0m ([38;5;153msrc/util.js:8-18[39m) is real by inspection, but [38;5;153mconfig.json[39m ships
  [38;5;153mretryAttempts: 3[39m and nothing sets 0. No trigger exists in the codebase — that's Minor, not Important.

  The Minor items (no [38;5;153mtotal[39m/[38;5;153mhasMore[39m in the response, test state leaking between cases because [38;5;153mseed()[39m is only called in
  the first test, JSDoc typing [38;5;153mpage[39m as [38;5;153mnumber[39m when query params arrive as strings, retry wrapper being dead weight over
  an in-memory [38;5;153mslice[39m) all check out as accurate and genuinely minor.

  [1mStrengths worth keeping[0m

  [38;5;153msrc/store.js:6[39m fixes a real latent bug from the base — [38;5;153mlistOrders()[39m used to hand out the live internal array.
  [38;5;153mparseOrderId[39m is well-shaped (anchored regex, [38;5;153mtypeof[39m guard, returns [38;5;153mnull[39m so the handler maps a clean 400). [38;5;153mwithRetry[39m's
  backoff arithmetic is correct.

  [1mVerdict[0m

  [1mNot ready to merge.[0m Two reachable critical defects in the headline feature, both invisible to the new tests.

